# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# This is not tidiness. GitHub Pages serves exactly the bytes git stores, which
# are LF, and scripts/version-assets.mjs stamps each asset's content hash onto
# every page so a changed file gets a new cache key. When a Windows working tree
# held CRLF and git held LF, that hash had TWO values for one unchanged file -
# styles.css was 8f6cff59 on a Windows desk and 337b86b3 in Linux CI - and the
# stamp oscillated between them, rewriting all 81 pages on each flip.
#
# versionOf now normalises before hashing, so the bug is fixed at the source.
# This file removes the divergence itself, so the next asset added here cannot
# reintroduce it: with core.autocrlf=input, git normalises on commit but leaves
# the working tree alone, which is how styles.css ended up as the only CRLF file
# in the repo.
#
# Committing this changes no stored content - every blob is already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
